    "created_at": "2016-04-26T16:37:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-26T16:37:40Z",
    "body": "Hmm.  I don't think https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/8a843f2169a6864a3024c4329528dccb2051d275 changed anything much here.  We still have https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#concept-origin defining the origin of a document dynamically in terms of the document's address, which is a mutable thing.  It does talk about it being a copy, but doesn't say when the copy is done (i.e. whether it's at some particular point in time or whether it's at the point when the Document is created or what).  Maybe that's the only remaining issue at this point and we should clarify that the origin is snapshotted at some early point and does not change when the document address changes.  Of course then we should just define it in terms of the URL the document is loaded from, whatever that's called, which is immutable, instead of the mutable document address.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
